    <div class="prose-dark">

      <h2>What Car Alpha Does</h2>
      <p>Car Alpha decodes Vehicle Identification Numbers using the official NHTSA VPIC database and cross-references decoded vehicles against the federal recall database in real time. We surface the data that matters: make, model, year, engine, trim, body type, drive configuration, plant of manufacture, and open safety recalls &mdash; all from a single 17-character input.</p>
      <p>Beyond raw data, we provide structured vehicle ownership intelligence across all 50 US states: <a href="/states/">state-specific insurance requirements</a>, lemon law protections, registration processes, and EV incentive programs. This information is compiled from official state sources and presented in a consumer-friendly format.</p>
      <p>We also built one of the few browser-based VIN scanners available on the open web. Using camera-based optical character recognition with frame consensus and check digit validation, the scanner lets users <a href="/learn/how-vin-decoding-works/#ocr-scanning">read VINs directly from the vehicle</a> without installing any app.</p>

      <h2>Why We Built This</h2>
      <p>The automotive data landscape is fragmented and extractive. Consumers researching a vehicle purchase are funneled through paywalled history reports, lead-generation insurance forms, and gated dealer inventories before they can access basic vehicle facts that are publicly available in federal databases. We believe that is wrong.</p>
      <p>Every piece of data in the NHTSA VPIC and Recalls databases is taxpayer-funded public information. VIN decoding, recall checking, and safety verification should not require a paid subscription or personal data exchange. Car Alpha makes these tools free, fast, and frictionless.</p>

      <h2>How We Make Money</h2>
      <p>Car Alpha earns revenue exclusively through affiliate partnerships. When a user decodes a VIN or researches a vehicle, we present optional next steps: comparing insurance rates, exploring warranty coverage, getting repair estimates, checking vehicle history, or reviewing loan offers. If a user clicks through to one of these partner services and takes action, we earn a commission.</p>
      <p>This model keeps Car Alpha free for consumers while maintaining sustainability. Critically:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>We never gate data behind affiliate links. VIN decoding, recall data, and all educational content are always free.</li>
        <li>Affiliate links are clearly labeled and disclosed on every page, in compliance with FTC guidelines (16 CFR Part 255).</li>
        <li>Editorial recommendations are independent of affiliate commissions. See our <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial Standards</a> for the full policy.</li>
      </ul>

