      <h2>Industry Recognition & Standards</h2>
      <p>Car Alpha adheres to the highest standards of data accuracy, consumer transparency, and editorial integrity in the automotive information industry.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>FTC Compliance:</strong> Full compliance with 16 CFR Part 255 (Guides Concerning the Use of Endorsements and Testimonials in Advertising). Every affiliate relationship is disclosed inline and on our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">Affiliate Disclosure</a> page.</li>
        <li><strong>Data Standards:</strong> VIN decoding follows ISO 3779 and ISO 3780 international standards, verified against 49 CFR Part 565 federal regulations.</li>
        <li><strong>Editorial Independence:</strong> Content recommendations are independent of affiliate partnerships. See our <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial Standards</a> for the complete policy.</li>
        <li><strong>Privacy:</strong> No user registration required. No VIN data stored. Camera-based VIN scanning processes entirely client-side with no server transmission of images or video frames.</li>
        <li><strong>Accessibility:</strong> Platform designed for keyboard navigation and screen reader compatibility. Reduced-motion support for users with vestibular sensitivities.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our Commitment</h2>
      <p>Car Alpha exists because we believe that fundamental vehicle safety and specification data should be free and accessible to everyone. The NHTSA databases we query are funded by taxpayers and maintained for public benefit. No consumer should need to pay a subscription fee or surrender personal information to access data that is already public.</p>
      <p>We are committed to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Keeping core tools permanently free</strong> &mdash; VIN decoding, recall checking, and vehicle education content will never be gated behind a paywall or account requirement.</li>
        <li><strong>Data accuracy</strong> &mdash; All vehicle specifications and recall data come from primary federal sources, queried in real time. We do not cache, modify, or interpolate NHTSA data.</li>
        <li><strong>Consumer protection</strong> &mdash; Our guides on <a href="/guides/how-vin-fraud-works/">VIN fraud detection</a>, <a href="/guides/hidden-salvage-title-warning-signs/">salvage title warning signs</a>, and <a href="/guides/how-to-check-car-before-buying/">used car inspection</a> are written to protect buyers, not to sell them products.</li>
        <li><strong>Transparency</strong> &mdash; Our <a href="/data-transparency/">Data Transparency</a> and <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> pages explain exactly how we source, process, and present every data point on this platform.</li>
